{"name":"Chocolate Milk","hex":"#976f4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate milk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweetened cocoa-flavored drink, typically created by mixing chocolate syrup or chocolate powder with milk, and typically served cold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate_milk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate milk","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate milk is a type of flavoured milk made by mixing cocoa powder with milk. It is a food pairing in which the milk's mouthfeel masks the dietary fibres of the (non-fat) cocoa solids of cocoa powder."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Chocolate_milk.JPG/330px-Chocolate_milk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_milk","wikidata":"Q13253"},{"title":"Chocolate Milk (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate Milk was an American funk and soul band from New Orleans, Louisiana, active in the 1970s and early 1980s."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_Milk_(band)","wikidata":"Q5103623"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk","wikidata":"Q8495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Chocomilkjf.JPG/500px-Chocomilkjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Chocomilkjf.JPG/1280px-Chocomilkjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Chocomilkjf.JPG/500px-Chocomilkjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of pasteurized chocolate milk made from water buffalo's milk produced by the Philippine Carabao Center","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocomilkjf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sir_Hans_Sloane_Hot_Chocolate.jpg/500px-Sir_Hans_Sloane_Hot_Chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sir_Hans_Sloane_Hot_Chocolate.jpg/500px-Sir_Hans_Sloane_Hot_Chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate milk recipe in the 1850s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASir_Hans_Sloane_Hot_Chocolate.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th